<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTD/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    BYAN macOS entitlements — F21.
    Required by hardenedRuntime: true in electron-builder.yml.

    com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit
      Electron uses V8 which JIT-compiles JavaScript. Without this,
      hardenedRuntime blocks the engine.

    com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory
      Some V8 sub-features still write to executable pages outside the
      JIT region; Electron documents this as required for Node integration.

    com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation
      Electron loads bundled .dylib files (e.g. keytar's native module)
      that are signed by us (or not signed at all in unsigned builds).
      The default library validation refuses to load anything that isn't
      signed by the same Team ID as the parent app.

    com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables
      Required for some Node native modules that rely on DYLD_* env vars.

    com.apple.security.network.client
      The renderer + main both make outgoing HTTPS requests to the byan_web
      API and to GitHub Releases (auto-update feed).

    com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write
      Onboarding lets the user pick a project root via the native file
      dialog; we then write to it (.claude/, .codex/, .github/, _byan/).
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
